@clawsweeper re-review

Cold Stop now persists before any tab exists, and current dashboard authority reaches every deferred batch effect, including nested `stopOnError:false`. The updated PR body includes real Gateway/Chromium proof with physical target closure deliberately unavailable: both Stop and replacement reject the old batch with zero forbidden clicks, while harmless control clicks prove the old page remains responsive.

The 42 SQLite board cases now explicitly cover legacy native identity adoption and preserved document grants/generations. All 465 Browser cases, targeted types/guards, independent P2 review, and the fresh OpenAI Tool Search HTTP-app replay pass. The current branch also includes the merged quota-status fix.

@clawsweeper re-review

The only change since the clean technical review is a proven startup regression repair: defer runtime.gateway access until dashboard use. The eager registration read caused broad runtime loading during a background model-runtime refresh. Paired main/candidate runs and the CPU profile attributed 159 seconds to that path; the same unchanged configuration-history case now takes 2.27 seconds, and all 79 configuration cases pass. The registration regression demonstrably failed before the repair; 71 Browser cases, full build/lint, independent P2 review, and a fresh cold Gateway/Chromium dashboard navigation replay pass.

The PR body also explicitly confirms config/data compatibility and the existing real-SQLite upgrade proof. Current head: 8deb4328990d75fb6fba0d2298d6bd10e73be9bd.

@clawsweeper re-review

The configuration shard now passes hosted CI. Since the last clean technical review, the only change is a 12-line temporary test-fixture update for the newer CI-owned aggregate boundary checker introduced by #146771. The fixture now supplies the canonical preload and records the new checker’s actual arguments, preserving the existing exact assertions. Red/green was proven against the newer main tooling, six focused candidate cases passed, lint/format passed, and independent review is clean through P2. Browser production code is unchanged.

Current head: da841079788409cf20c2b618a4614c90a7bbe72e.
